From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Łukasz Buśko <lukasz.busko@guns4hire.cc>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt7988a-bpi-r4-pro-8x: hog switch reset high

The MxL86252C 2.5G switch of the BPi-R4 Pro 8X is held in reset by its
HRSTN line, which is MT7988 GPIO 4 (GPIO_A). Nothing in the upstream board
description claims that pin, so it is left in its reset default and is also
free for userspace: one `gpioset gpiochip0 4=0` drops the whole switch -
CPU port included - and the board becomes unreachable with no way back but
a power cycle.

The Bananapi vendor tree keeps the line high with a gpio-hog ("MxL86252C
2.5G switch reset pin GPIO4: High"). Do the same here: the hog takes the
pin when the pinctrl driver registers its gpio chip, so the switch is
guaranteed to come out of reset on every boot, and gpiolib refuses the
line to userspace afterwards.

Based on the BPi-R4 Pro 8X board support from the Bananapi vendor tree.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts |  9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
@@ -166,3 +166,12 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+&pio {
+	/* MxL86252C switch reset (GPIO_A): keep the switch out of reset */
+	switch-hrstn-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <4 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+	};
+};
